- Connected to F5 VPN
- Logged into [Panorama](https://panorama-sbox-uks-0.sandbox.platform.hmcts.net)
- Monitor > Logs shows traffic to your VM IP
- Traffic shows "Action: allow" (not deny)

**5. SSH Access to VM**

Connected to VPN, SSH to bastion:
```bash
az ssh vm -n bastion-sbox -g bastion-sbox-rg --subscription DTS-MANAGEMENT-SBOX-INTSVC
```

From bastion, curl your VM:
```bash
curl <your-vm-private-ip>
```
Returns Apache HTML

SSH to your VM:
```bash
ssh labsAdmin2023@<your-vm-private-ip>
```
Successfully logs in

**6. Browser Access**

- Open browser (not on VPN if testing public access)
- Navigate to: `https://labs-goldenpath-<yourname>.sandbox.platform.hmcts.net`
- See Apache default page or your custom content
- SSL certificate valid (no browser warnings)
- Page loads within a few seconds (Front Door caching works)


**Congratulations!** 

You've successfully:

- Created VNet infrastructure with proper peering and routing
- Configured firewall rules for network security
- Set up DNS and Front Door for public access
- Gained hands-on experience with the full HMCTS network stack

You're now ready to move on to the [AKS Cluster](./aks-cluster.html) section!

